<!-- ══════════ PAGE: ABOUT ══════════ -->
<div class="page" id="page-about">

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-label">Institution</div>
    <div class="section-title">About SRM Institute of Science and Technology</div>
    <div class="section-rule"></div>
    <div class="text-content">
      <p>SRM Institute of Science and Technology is one of India's leading multidisciplinary higher education institutions, recognized for excellence in teaching, research, innovation, and industry engagement. Established with a vision to impart quality education and foster technological advancement, SRMIST offers comprehensive programmes across Engineering, Management, Medicine, Science, Law, Agricultural Sciences, and Allied Health Sciences.</p>
      <p>In NIRF 2025, SRMIST achieved the <strong>22nd rank Overall</strong> and <strong>11th among universities</strong> in India, reflecting its commitment to quality higher education and research excellence.</p>
      <p>With campuses in Kattankulathur (Chennai), Ramapuram, Vadapalani, Tiruchirappalli, Modinagar, Sonepat, Amaravati, and Gangtok, SRMIST has established itself as a nationally recognized centre of excellence. The university attracts students from across India and many countries, creating a vibrant multicultural environment.</p>
    </div>
    <img src="campus-top-view.png" alt="SRM Tiruchirappalli Campus Aerial View" class="section-img">
    <p class="img-caption">Aerial view of SRM Institute of Science and Technology, Tiruchirappalli Campus</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-alt">
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-label">Department</div>
      <div class="section-title">Department of Computer Science and Engineering</div>
      <div class="section-rule"></div>
      <div class="two-col">
        <div class="text-content">
          <p>The Department of CSE at SRMIST Tiruchirappalli was established in 2021 with the vision of imparting quality education and fostering innovation in computing. It promotes research in Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Data Science, Cyber Security, Cloud Computing, and the Internet of Things.</p>
          <p>The department collaborates with leading organizations through internships, workshops, expert talks, and industry-driven projects, bridging academia and industry effectively.</p>
          <div class="about-img-col" style="margin-top:16px;">
            <img src="class-view.png" alt="Classroom and Lab Facilities">
            <img src="campus-student.png" alt="Students at SRM Campus">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="card" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
            <h3>Vision</h3>
            <p>To provide quality education in Computer Science and Engineering and produce highly competent engineers who can serve society on a global level.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Mission</h3>
            <p>To provide industry-oriented training that prepares graduates for real-world challenges, while emphasising ethical conduct and social responsibility.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-label">Conference Scope &amp; Objective</div>
    <div class="section-title">Objective and Scope of the Conference</div>
    <div class="section-rule"></div>
    <div class="text-content">
      <p><strong>Objective of the Conference:</strong> ETCSIS 2027 aims to provide an international platform for researchers, academicians, industry professionals, research scholars and students to exchange knowledge and present innovative research in Computer Science and Intelligent Systems.</p>
      <p><strong>Conference Scope:</strong> The conference scope covers AI &amp; Machine Learning, Generative AI, Data Science, Cybersecurity, Cloud and Edge Computing, IoT, Software Engineering, Computer Networks, Blockchain, Human-Centered Computing, Quantum Computing, Robotics, Autonomous Systems and Sustainable Computing — aiming to develop secure, intelligent, scalable and sustainable solutions for next-generation computing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="notice" style="margin-top: 28px;">
      <strong>International Advisory Board:</strong> SRM's IAB, established in 2003, consists of 50+ distinguished deans, directors, and professors from Harvard Business School, MIT, Stanford, LSE, UC Berkeley, Cambridge, NUS, and many more of the world's leading institutions. View the <a href="#" class="inline-link" onclick="showPage('committee',document.querySelectorAll('nav a')[4])">International Advisory Board members</a> on the Committee page.
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

